// Back: a clean stroked chevron.
//
// This replaces a "dotted chevron" built from 2.86-unit blocks. That staircase
// was the point of the old glyph, but 2.86 is not a whole number of pixels at
// any common scale, so every block edge landed mid-pixel and the arrow read as
// low-resolution rather than as deliberate pixel art.
//
// TWO CANVAS REPS. Chromium picks the rep matching the requested size, so the
// 16 rep is drawn at 16 rather than scaled down from 24 -- which is what
// actually makes it crisp in the toolbar. Coordinates in each rep are whole or
// half units so the stroke sits on the pixel grid.
//
// FLIPS_IN_RTL: a back arrow points the other way in right-to-left locales,
// and the old glyph never did.
//
// CENTRED IN THE CANVAS, which the first version was not: it spanned x 8..15,
// centre 11.5 against a canvas centre of 12, and forward was its mirror so it
// leaned the other way. Half a unit each, in opposite directions, is enough to
// see -- the pair read as splayed apart inside containers that were themselves
// perfectly centred, which is exactly what made it look like a layout bug.
//
// Both reps are now a 45-degree chevron on WHOLE units, centred on both axes:
// 24 spans 9..15 and 6..18, 16 spans 6..10 and 4..12. Keep it that way. If the
// size needs changing, change it symmetrically about the canvas centre.

CANVAS_DIMENSIONS, 24,
FLIPS_IN_RTL,
STROKE, 2.f,
CAP_SQUARE,
MOVE_TO, 15, 6,
LINE_TO, 9, 12,
LINE_TO, 15, 18,
CLOSE

CANVAS_DIMENSIONS, 16,
FLIPS_IN_RTL,
STROKE, 1.5f,
CAP_SQUARE,
MOVE_TO, 10, 4,
LINE_TO, 6, 8,
LINE_TO, 10, 12,
CLOSE
